@page "/"

<PageTitle>OllamaProxy Admin</PageTitle>

@* Page wrapper: caps and centers the welcome content at the layout width. The shell container is width-neutral,
   so without this wrapper the hero band would stretch across the full canvas. *@
<div class="home-page">
	@* Welcome hero: a dark navy band echoing the shell header (#16213e) so the logo's own dark backdrop sits on a
	   matching surface instead of clashing with the otherwise-light admin theme. The logo is framed as a glowing
	   rounded tile, which reads as an intentional element and hides the square image edge. *@
	<section class="home-hero">
		<div class="home-hero-logo">
			<OllamaProxyLogo ShouldBlink="true"
			                 aria-label="OllamaProxy logo: a llama face, one half a glowing circuit board, the other a clean white silhouette"/>
		</div>
		<p class="home-hero-tagline">Speak Ollama, run OpenAI.</p>
	</section>

	<h1 class="home-about-title">About this project</h1>

	<p class="home-lead">
		OllamaProxy is a lightweight reverse proxy that exposes the <strong>Ollama API</strong> while forwarding and
		translating every request to one or more <strong>OpenAI-compatible backends</strong> — so any Ollama-aware
		client can reach cloud or local models, with per-model routing.
	</p>

	@* Project links: external resources rather than runtime state, so they open in a new tab and carry rel="noopener"
	   to keep the admin tab isolated from the opened page. Branch-agnostic GitHub URLs (#readme, blob/HEAD) survive a
	   default-branch rename. *@
	<ul class="home-links">
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/LumaCoreTech/OllamaProxy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Project home</a>
			<span class="home-link-note">Source, releases and discussion on GitHub</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/LumaCoreTech/OllamaProxy/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Issue tracker</a>
			<span class="home-link-note">Report a bug or request a feature</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/LumaCoreTech/OllamaProxy#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Documentation</a>
			<span class="home-link-note">Configuration, endpoints and example setups</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="https://github.com/LumaCoreTech/OllamaProxy/blob/HEAD/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">License</a>
			<span class="home-link-note">MIT — free and open source for everyone</span>
		</li>
	</ul>
</div>
